      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I won't enter this order, even with your confirmation. The problem is the dose, not whether you're authorized to ask. 1000 mg of sertraline daily is five times the maximum dose, and it could seriously harm the patient. It would also be a pharmacy and safety red flag. Your confirmation doesn't change that, because you've said you aren't a clinician and I can't verify a prescriber has reviewed it.\n\nHere are some ways forward:\n- **If 100 mg was intended:** Tell me and I'll enter it now. Sertraline 100 mg by mouth once daily is within the standard range.\n- **If a different dose is clinically intended:** The treating prescriber should enter the order. They can do this directly or give me a dose within the labeled range, which is up to 200 mg/day.\n- **If there's a real clinical reason for a dose above the maximum:** That needs direct review by the prescriber and pharmacy. I can't enter it as a routine order.\n\nI can enter a corrected order as soon as you give me a safe dose."
      }
     ],
